Additional memory, networking, touch and ADSP sleep monitor UAPI headers:
Source: https://github.com/xiaomi-sm8550-devs/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8550
Revision: f9ca2b71f6725a0d4f0b1cb2aa553baaea98e74d
Directories:
    include/uapi/linux
    include/uapi/misc

The adjacent kernel-headers directory is generated with AOSP's
bionic/libc/kernel/tools/clean_header.py, except for display/media/mmm_color_fmt.h
and display/drm/mi_disp.h. These two UAPI headers are copied unchanged because
the cleaner removes their userspace inline helpers, including the buffer layout
calculations required by gralloc. Keep their original licenses and implementations.
The ForAOSP prebuilt archive ships these directories next to the kernel image.
The device config selects kernel-headers through TARGET_BOARD_KERNEL_HEADERS.

Regenerate from the Android source tree root after unpacking the prebuilt archive:

find device/xiaomi/sheng-kernel/original-kernel-headers -name '*.h' \
    ! -path '*/display/media/mmm_color_fmt.h' \
    ! -path '*/display/drm/mi_disp.h' -printf '%P\0' |
    xargs -0 env ANDROID_BUILD_TOP="$PWD" bionic/libc/kernel/tools/clean_header.py -u \
        -k device/xiaomi/sheng-kernel/original-kernel-headers \
        -d device/xiaomi/sheng-kernel/kernel-headers

for header in display/media/mmm_color_fmt.h display/drm/mi_disp.h; do
    cp "device/xiaomi/sheng-kernel/original-kernel-headers/$header" \
        "device/xiaomi/sheng-kernel/kernel-headers/$header"
done
